> Jorge Llamb=C3=ADas scripsit:
>
> > That was the idea, yes. In fact only Cyr and Cyn. The -l- hyphen would
> now
> > never be needed, since the final consonant of the rafsi becomes
> irrelevant
> > for the choice of hyphen and so -yr- works for all cases except when th=
e
> > fu'ivla proper begins with r.
>
> I was actually thinking of something more radical:  replace all syllabic
> consonants with yC throughout the language.


OK, the effect would be the same, since outside of cmevla the only syllabic
consonants that could survive would be the type-3 fu'ivla hyphens (the rest
would have to go because fu'ivla can't have y). In cmevla camxes already
allows y-syllables with codas.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

